186321155 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534938 true] [17592186321155 1100 "The minimum value of the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321155 1113 #uuid "794a2260-974a-5a5a-af52-bb91dcf1ebd2" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321155 1145 "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/assets/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the minimum value of the function is $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321157 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321158 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321159 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321160 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321161 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1041 "selection" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321161 13194139534938 true] [17592186321156 1110 #uuid "7a419ac6-8070-557e-89c9-36a16c0427e5" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321157 1034 "There is no minimum value" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534938 true] [17592186321157 1111 #uuid "9e588f20-ef86-59dc-b62d-12450320dfef" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321158 1034 "-2\\pi " 13194139534938 true] [17592186321158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321158 1111 #uuid "d0130e26-5716-5576-bccb-4a079be6c23e" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321159 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321159 1111 #uuid "2cb74260-e1ac-53b3-aaf8-07c5aaab753a" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321160 1034 "-\\pi " 13194139534938 true] [17592186321160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321160 1111 #uuid "7af40bf4-e02b-5faa-a7f1-7ad58226c461" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321161 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321161 1111 #uuid "63f214f1-3138-58b7-ab40-ee1317c611bb" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321162 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321163 13194139534938 true] [17592186321162 1089 "q-7338" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321162 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534938 true] [17592186321162 1100 "Express $8{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-4$ as a single trigonometric ratio." 13194139534938 true] [17592186321162 1113 #uuid "33594db7-6d24-536b-a84c-855f2f373c65" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321162 1145 "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n4(2{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-1)\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2{cos}^{2}⁡{15}^{∘}-1) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321164 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321165 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321166 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321167 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321168 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1041 "selection" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321165 13194139534938 true] [17592186321163 1110 #uuid "26cbde72-b856-544f-a548-9b54f3b0231b" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321164 1034 "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321164 1111 #uuid "ef6ef49e-98bb-5466-b00a-d02e9e8f0544" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321165 1034 "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321165 1111 #uuid "88231c56-e258-5fd9-b5c4-f579da9eefe4" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321166 1034 "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321166 1111 #uuid "1f5c3c9e-99b7-5caa-8971-f3c3bb3601d7" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321167 1034 "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321167 1111 #uuid "2b7a48c5-07e9-5e4c-8dee-377c497be27e" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321168 1034 "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321168 1111 #uuid "54643908-4cd0-5504-adfc-d57785d735a8" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321169 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321170 13194139534938 true] [17592186321169 1089 "q-89052" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321169 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534938 true] [17592186321169 1100 "A pet center offers veterinary services to dogs and cats. Of the total patients, $\\frac{3}{5}$\nare dogs and $\\frac{2}{5}$ are cats. Also, $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the dogs are vaccinated while $\\frac{7}{15}$ of all pets are vaccinated. What is the probability that a randomly selected cat assisted by the center is vaccinated?" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321169 1113 #uuid "993a5199-6dff-5393-ad8f-667e046f8498" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321169 1142 true 13194139534938 true] [17592186321169 1145 "Let $V$ be the event that the chosen pet is vaccinated, and let $D$ be the event that the pet is a dog. Then ${D}^{′}$ is the event that the pet is a cat.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected pet is vaccinated, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(V)=P(V|D)P(D)+P(V|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{3}{5}$ of the pets in the center are dogs and $\\frac{2}{5}$ are cats, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=\\frac{3}{5},\\,P({D}^{′})=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the dogs are vaccinated, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|D)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{7}{15}$ of the pets are vaccinated, we have\n\n$$\nP(V)=\\frac{7}{15}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(V|{D}^{′})$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(V) & =P(V|D)P(D)+P(V|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{15} & =(\\frac{1}{3})(\\frac{3}{5})+P(V|{D}^{′})(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ \\frac{7}{15} & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}P(V|{D}^{′}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}P(V|{D}^{′}) & =\\frac{7-3}{15} \\\\ P(V|{D}^{′}) & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected cat assisted in the center is vaccinated is $\\frac{2}{3}.$" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321171 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321172 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321173 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321174 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321175 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1041 "selection" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321171 13194139534938 true] [17592186321170 1110 #uuid "0806ce5c-aacd-57fa-ad36-4fa5e71bdd78" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321171 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321171 1111 #uuid "8ba3c1ac-1ca3-53f9-9308-5dbed69fe9b7" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321172 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139534938 true] [17592186321172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534938 true] [17592186321172 1111 #uuid "38d4d7e0-5da4-5645-b006-8c7f1c360922" 131941395349